  "title": "Only standing waves persist on Sierpinski tetrahedra",
  "subject": "Which signed laws reproduce themselves on Sierpinski tetrahedra and four-simplices, and where the standing wave fails",
  "conclusion": "The cosine wave (-1)^(x_0) cos(theta E) reproduces itself exactly when the number of simplices is odd and otherwise turns into the sine wave, which explains the period-4 family of the plane. In exact censuses on Sierpinski tetrahedra and four-simplices the only knots exact at every computed level are standing waves, and the wave's rational exceptional angles are only pi/2 and, at even levels, pi/4.",
